WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the spoken Hinglish, not a verbatim transcript. Cue timing is automatically aligned and is not human-verified; it can still be wrong.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700 line:0% position:50% align:center
In Batch 3 we study Daily Allowance and claims.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.760 line:0% position:50% align:center
The focus is Central Government civilian official travel.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.440 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a Level 7 officer checks train, hotel and food
separately.

4
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.700 line:0% position:50% align:center
Examples are hypothetical; verify the latest order and
sanction.

5
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.230 line:0% position:50% align:center
Important correction: the earlier batches missed this train
order.

6
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.390 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check the DoE order of 30 August 2023.

7
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.090 line:0% position:50% align:center
Vande Bharat has the corresponding Shatabdi entitlement.

8
00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.910 line:0% position:50% align:center
Humsafar has the corresponding Rajdhani entitlement.

9
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.050 line:0% position:50% align:center
It applies to tour, training, transfer and retirement
journeys.

10
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.830 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, Level 7 checks its eligible chair-car class.

11
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.560 line:0% position:50% align:center
Food-component bills do not have to be submitted.

12
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:45.120 line:0% position:50% align:center
The percentage depends on absence during each calendar day.

13
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.180 line:0% position:50% align:center
Under six hours is 30%; six to twelve hours is 70%.

14
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.600 line:0% position:50% align:center
Above twelve hours is 100%.

15
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.600 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, seven hours at Level 7 gives ₹700 for food.

16
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.530 line:0% position:50% align:center
Count absence separately for each midnight-to-midnight day.

17
00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:03.590 line:0% position:50% align:center
Example: a Level 7 tour runs from 8 p.m. to 5 a.m.

18
00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.450 line:0% position:50% align:center
The first day has four hours and the next day five hours.

19
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.930 line:0% position:50% align:center
Both attract 30%: ₹300 plus ₹300.

20
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:13.910 line:0% position:50% align:center
The total food component is ₹600, subject to the conditions.

21
00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.520 line:0% position:50% align:center
If both boarding and lodging are free, consult the special
rule.

22
00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.780 line:0% position:50% align:center
The old 25% Daily Allowance is discontinued.

23
00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.320 line:0% position:50% align:center
Eligible local travel expenditure may be claimed under the
rules.

24
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.960 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, an official city ride cost ₹200.

25
00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:34.040 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check entitlement and proof before claiming that actual
expense.

26
00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.890 line:0% position:50% align:center
A free breakfast alone is not the same as both facilities
being free.

27
00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:41.930 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not assume a fixed percentage for partial meals from this
order.

28
00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:45.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, breakfast is free but dinner is paid by the
officer.

29
00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.430 line:0% position:50% align:center
Confirm the specific applicable instruction with the accounts
office.

30
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.140 line:0% position:50% align:center
The hotel ceiling is a maximum, not an automatic payment.

31
00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:56.840 line:0% position:50% align:center
The general rule allows self-certification through Level 8.

32
00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.860 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a Level 7 officer has an eligible room cost of
₹800.

33
00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:03.720 line:0% position:50% align:center
The room claim is ₹800, not the full ceiling.

34
00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.560 line:0% position:50% align:center
The higher Class X city limit requires vouchers.

35
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.250 line:0% position:50% align:center
Hotel taxes may be reimbursed above the entitlement.

36
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.710 line:0% position:50% align:center
GST is calculated on the eligible actual charge.

37
00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:17.290 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, ₹800 room cost and a hypothetical 12% tax.

38
00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:21.170 line:0% position:50% align:center
Tax is ₹96 and total ₹896, subject to the other conditions.

39
00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check the actual GST rate and invoice with accounts.

40
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.240 line:0% position:50% align:center
City travel at Levels 9 to 11 has a voucher waiver.

41
00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:32.320 line:0% position:50% align:center
The self-certification records the travel period and vehicle
number.

42
00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.780 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a Level 10 eligible non-AC ride costs ₹350.

43
00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:41.460 line:0% position:50% align:center
Claim the actual expense, not a fixed ceiling payment.

44
00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:45.780 line:0% position:50% align:center
An older clarification discusses airport transfers separately.

45
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.460 line:0% position:50% align:center
Verify its current application with the accounts office.

46
00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:53.840 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, airport-to-hotel and hotel-to-meeting are
distinct rides.

47
00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.020 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not claim the same ride twice.

48
00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.920 line:0% position:50% align:center
For a local journey, check distance from the normal duty
point.

49
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
Government training material describes an eight-kilometre
radius test.

50
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:08.760 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a temporary office lies outside eight kilometres
from the normal office.

51
00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.540 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not decide solely from the distance from home.

52
00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:16.390 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, Level 7 and seven hours gives ₹350.

53
00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.950 line:0% position:50% align:center
But an authenticated original of the 2018 letter was not
located.

54
00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:23.190 line:0% position:50% align:center
Therefore confirm with accounts before making an actual claim.

55
00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:28.030 line:0% position:50% align:center
There is a clause for specified scientific and data-collection
fieldwork.

56
00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.270 line:0% position:50% align:center
The rate may be equivalent to the food component.

57
00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:35.230 line:0% position:50% align:center
Approval from the Head of Department or controlling officer is
required.

58
00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:39.650 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a remote survey team travels on foot or by mule.

59
00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not treat every ship journey as an automatic extra payment.

60
00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.520 line:0% position:50% align:center
The base rate for a foot journey was ₹12 per kilometre.

61
00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.820 line:0% position:50% align:center
After the first 25% increase it is ₹15.

62
00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:53.920 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, four eligible kilometres were actually walked.

63
00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:57.300 line:0% position:50% align:center
Four times fifteen is ₹60; check the conditions.

64
00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:02.030 line:0% position:50% align:center
Keep sanction, level, journey dates and tickets in the claim
pack.

65
00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:04.490 line:0% position:50% align:center
Hotel and city-travel documentation rules are different.

66
00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:09.150 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, Level 10 keeps the hotel receipt and
self-certifies the city ride.

67
00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.430 line:0% position:50% align:center
Separate food vouchers are not required for the food
component.

68
00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.910 line:0% position:50% align:center
Also retain acknowledgement of submission.

69
00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:18.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
If a tour boarding pass is missing, consult the prescribed
declaration.

70
00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.220 line:0% position:50% align:center
At Level 10 and below the controlling officer countersigns.

71
00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:26.060 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a Level 10 officer fills the form and gets it
countersigned.

72
00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:29.520 line:0% position:50% align:center
Honestly declare the actual journey and absence of a duplicate
claim.

73
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:34.010 line:0% position:50% align:center
The claim limit for tour, transfer and training is 60 days.

74
00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:37.210 line:0% position:50% align:center
The order changed retirement claims to 180 days.

75
00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.730 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check the rule starting from the day after the journey.

76
00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:45.530 line:0% position:50% align:center
A 1 March tour makes the claim due for payment on 2 March, not
the filing deadline.

77
00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:49.450 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not wait until the last day; a late claim may be forfeited.

78
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:53.560 line:0% position:50% align:center
If you are your own controlling officer, check Treasury or
Cash Section.

79
00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.400 line:0% position:50% align:center
In other cases submit to the Head of Office or controlling
officer.

80
00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.060 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, an officer submits on time to the Head of Office.

81
00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.560 line:0% position:50% align:center
A dated acknowledgement can establish the submission date.

82
00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:07.860 line:0% position:50% align:center
Review of abeyance over one year is not an automatic waiver.

83
00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:11.670 line:0% position:50% align:center
If a tour advance was taken, check a separate deadline.

84
00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:15.570 line:0% position:50% align:center
Compendium Rule 51 specifies adjustment within 15 days.

85
00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:19.530 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check the date of tour completion or resumption of duty after
it.

86
00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:23.590 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, an officer with an advance submits an adjustment
bill promptly.

87
00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.510 line:0% position:50% align:center
Recovery or interest may apply if it is late.

88
00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:30.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
Some rates rose when Dearness Allowance reached 50%.

89
00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.920 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, Level 7 food increased from ₹800 to ₹1,000.

90
00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:37.960 line:0% position:50% align:center
A DA of 60% does not by itself trigger a second increase.

91
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.900 line:0% position:50% align:center
Verify later orders, service rules and open exceptions.

92
00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.120 line:0% position:50% align:center
The detailed guide and source ledger contain the examples.
